{"id": "section-body-10856", "title": "Prelabour Rupture of Membranes (PROM)", "chapterId": "chapter-eleven", "blocks": [{"id": "body-10856", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading2", "text": "Prelabour Rupture of Membranes (PROM)", "runs": [{"text": "Prelabour"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Rupture"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Membranes"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PROM)"}], "level": 2, "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1452"}}, {"id": "body-10857", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "It is the rupture of membranes (breakage of the amniotic sac) before the onset of labor. If rupture occurs before 37weeks it is called preterm prelabour rupture of membranes (PPROM). Prolonged PROM is a case of premature rupture of membranes in which more than 24 hours have passed between the rupture and the onset of labour. Prolonged PROM for more than 18 hours is a risk of ascending infection which can lead to chorioamnionitis (infection of chorion, amnion and amniotic fluid.", "runs": [{"text": "It is the rupture of membranes (breakage of the amniotic sac) before the onset of labor. If rupture occurs before 37weeks it"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is called preterm prelabour rupture of membranes (PPROM). Prolonged PROM is a case of premature rupture of membranes in which"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "more"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "than"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "24"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hours"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "have"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "passed"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "between"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rupture"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "onset"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "labour."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Prolonged"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "PROM"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "more"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "than"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "18"}, {"text": " "